---
import { doc, repo } from '../lib/content'
const tracks = [
  ['01', 'Enrollment API', 'Routes, identity boundaries and cross-account access checks.'],
  ['02', 'Host lifecycle', 'Readiness, heartbeats, graceful shutdown and recovery.'],
  ['03', 'Desktop live status', 'Live updates, reconnects and signed-out safety.'],
  ['04', 'Docs & roadmap', 'What exists, what is decided, and what is still a design question.'],
]
---

<section id="swarm" class="section mission-section" aria-labelledby="mission-title">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Real work / Phosphor Remote Hosts</p><h2 id="mission-title">
          An ambitious feature.<br />Not one giant prompt.
        </h2>
      </div>
      <p class="section-intro">
        One parent coordinated four workstreams. Workers asked before crossing their scope.
        Independent reviewers challenged the results. The parent owned integration.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="mission-tracks">
      {
        tracks.map(([number, title, text]) => (
          <article>
            <>
              <span class="mono">{number} / WORKSTREAM</span>
              <h3>{title}</h3>
              <p>{text}</p>
            </>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>
    <div class="mission-evidence">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The part a chat log doesn’t show</p><h3>
          A team you can<br />actually inspect.
        </h3>
      </div>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>Scope is explicit.</strong> A worker needed to change shared shutdown code. The parent
          approved a narrow exception and required existing behavior to stay tested.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Review is a separate job.</strong> Security, correctness and documentation reviews ran
          independently. “Finished” was not treated as “accepted.”
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>A failed run need not mean lost work.</strong> After a worker connection failure, a
          replacement continued from retained work and the recorded decisions.
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <div class="source-line">
      <a class="text-link" href={`${repo}/pull/427`}>Schema #427 ↗</a><a
        class="text-link"
        href={`${repo}/pull/429`}>Desktop approval #429 ↗</a
      ><a class="text-link" href={`${repo}/pull/435`}>Host identity #435 ↗</a><a
        class="text-link"
        href="/guides/swarm/#case-study">Read the case study →</a
      >
    </div>
    <p class="fineprint">
      The capture above replays selected, redacted records in the real Phosphor UI. Task labels are
      expanded; activity is historical, not live. This lane predates the Swarm switch. Remote Hosts
      is the feature being built, not a claim that remote execution is available.
    </p>

    <div class="team-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Your models. Your division of labor.</p><h3 class="subheading">
        Different minds.<br />One accountable workflow.
      </h3><p>
        The recorded parent used Astra and Opus 5.5 at different points; Sol 6.1 was assigned to
        workers and reviewers. Here is one way to divide a new mission.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="model-team" aria-label="Illustrative model roles, not automatic routing">
      <article>
        <span class="mono">EXPLORE & PLAN</span><h3>Astra</h3><p>
          Map the codebase, examine dependencies, and turn an open question into bounded work.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="mono">ORCHESTRATE & INTEGRATE</span><h3>Opus 5.5</h3><p>
          Delegate the pieces, answer scope questions, weigh review findings, and assemble the
          result.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="mono">IMPLEMENT & REVIEW</span><h3>Sol 6.1</h3><p>
          Build focused changes. Use separate reviewer runs to challenge them before integration.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <p class="fineprint">
      Example roles, not built-in presets or a benchmark. Choose available models and thinking
      levels through pi and pi-subagents. Phosphor does not automatically assign these models.
      Claude subscriptions can connect through pi-claude-cli.
    </p>
    <aside class="swarm-authorization">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">New / per-lane Swarm authorization</p><h3>
          Let the parent delegate.<br />Keep the work visible.
        </h3>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          Turn on <strong>Swarm</strong> to authorize proactive delegation when useful. The parent still
          decides whether a task needs a team. The switch is authorization, not a “start four agents”
          button.
        </p><p>
          Turning it off removes that standing authorization from future requests. It does not stop
          existing children or erase history. Old lanes need a Pi reload or restart to acquire the
          command.
        </p><a class="action action-text" href="/guides/swarm/"
          >Work with a swarm <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a
        ><a class="text-link" href={doc('chat.md#swarm-authorization')}
          >Exact behavior and boundaries ↗</a
        >
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</section>
<style>
  .mission-section {
    background: var(--px-sidebar);
  }
  .mission-tracks,
  .model-team {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
    border-block: 1px solid var(--px-border-strong);
  }
  .mission-tracks article,
  .model-team article {
    padding: 1.8rem 1.4rem;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--px-border);
  }
  article:last-child {
    border-right: 0;
  }
  article .mono {
    color: var(--px-accent);
  }
  article h3 {
    margin: 1rem 0 0.75rem;
  }
  article p {
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }
  .mission-evidence {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.7fr;
    gap: 4rem;
    padding-top: 3rem;
  }
  .mission-evidence h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
  }
  .mission-evidence ol {
    list-style: decimal;
    margin: 0;
    padding-left: 1.3rem;
    color: var(--px-text-secondary);
  }
  .mission-evidence li {
    padding: 0 0 1rem 0.6rem;
  }
  .mission-evidence li::marker {
    color: var(--px-accent);
    font-family: var(--px-font-mono);
  }
  .team-heading {
    margin-top: 5rem;
    max-width: 48rem;
  }
  .team-heading > p:last-child {
    margin: 1.4rem 0 2rem;
  }
  .model-team {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
  }
  .model-team h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
  }
  .swarm-authorization {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.3fr;
    gap: 3rem;
    padding: 2.5rem;
    margin-top: 3rem;
    background: var(--px-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--px-border-strong);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--px-accent);
  }
  .swarm-authorization h3 {
    font-size: var(--text-3xl);
  }
  .swarm-authorization p {
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
  }
  .swarm-authorization .text-link {
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    display: block;
  }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .mission-tracks {
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    }
    .mission-tracks article {
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--px-border);
    }
    .mission-tracks article:nth-child(2n) {
      border-right: 0;
    }
    .mission-evidence,
    .swarm-authorization {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 1.5rem;
    }
    .swarm-authorization {
      padding: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 480px) {
    .mission-tracks,
    .model-team {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
    .mission-tracks article,
    .model-team article {
      border-right: 0;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--px-border);
    }
  }
</style>
